 kit changes - lists each open change's reviews and checks, and the changes merged last

   one of
   *kit changes*  lists each open change's reviews and checks, and the changes merged last

     --text   --json   --jq
                           prints the stages as text, even on a terminal

   --stages     prints the stages, one per line, in order, the same over any workspace
   --marks      prints a mark per stage, as one JSON object, which changes when what the stage draws
                does: for each, the forge's own marks of its issues, which move with its changes,
                and of its runs
   reviews      {change, title, login, state, at, unresolved}, keyed by the change's number and the
                login: state is requested while the reviewer is asked and has not answered, else
                approved, changes, or commented; at is when they answered, in seconds since the
                epoch, null while asked and on Azure DevOps, whose votes have no time; unresolved
                counts the change's unresolved threads. The author's own comments are no review
   checks       {change, title, name, verdict, at, took}, keyed by the change's number and the
                check's name: verdict is passed, failed, or pending; at is when the run started, in
                seconds since the epoch, or null; took is how long it ran, in seconds, null while it
                runs. A forge whose provider lacks check-runs, as one written to a contract before
                4, has no runs on its changes: the document has no rows, and {feature: check-runs,
                off: true, lacked: true} under errors
   merged       {number, title, author, branch, merged, by}, keyed by its number: merged is when, in
                seconds since the epoch, and by who merged it; the title links to its page. Where
                the forge holds more, the document is limited, at how many it drew: a forge that
                lists them by update, as GitHub does, keeps only those merged since the oldest
                update it read, as one merged before may be missing
   changes      a tab kit flow prints; on a terminal it opens in kittui, and with a form it is
                refused


 kit changes
